{"title":"Career Roadmap · Gemologist","role":"Gemologist","summary":"A Gemologist identifies, evaluates, grades, tests, and documents gemstones and related materials. In the jewellery industry, the role combines gemstone identification, gemmological testing, colour and clarity assessment, treatments, valuation knowledge, jewellery-market awareness, and ethical sourcing.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Jewellery / Accessory Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For this career, a B.Des in Jewellery/Accessory Design provides useful design and jewellery-industry exposure, but specialised gemmological training is essential for professional gem-testing work. A design degree by itself does not make someone a gemologist."},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Jewellery/Accessory Design","Gemmology Training","Gemmology Internship/Trainee","Junior Gemologist","Gemologist","Senior Gemologist / Gem Lab Specialist","Gemmology Manager / Technical Specialist"],"label":"Typical route"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Approx. Timeline","Target"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Jewellery + material fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Gem Knowledge"},{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Gemstone identification + properties"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Testing + treatments + grading"}],[{"text":"Industry Preparation"},{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Gemmology training + internship"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Gemmology Trainee / Junior Gemologist"}],[{"text":"Growth"},{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Gemologist"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"6–10 years"},{"text":"Senior Gemologist / Lab Specialist"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"10–15 years"},{"text":"Gem Lab Manager / Technical Head"}],[{"text":"Long-term"},{"text":"15+ years"},{"text":"Senior Gemmology Sp