nd":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Core Skills","Potential Roles"],"rows":[[{"text":"Diamond Grading"},{"text":"4Cs + diamond testing"},{"text":"Diamond Grader"}],[{"text":"Coloured Stones"},{"text":"Ruby, sapphire, emerald etc."},{"text":"Coloured Stone Gemologist"}],[{"text":"Gem Identification"},{"text":"Instruments + microscopy"},{"text":"Gemologist"}],[{"text":"Gemstone Treatments"},{"text":"Treatment detection"},{"text":"Treatment Specialist"}],[{"text":"Gem Lab"},{"text":"Testing + reporting"},{"text":"Laboratory Gemologist"}],[{"text":"Jewellery QA"},{"text":"Gem + jewellery inspection"},{"text":"Quality Specialist"}],[{"text":"Gem Valuation"},{"text":"Gemology + market knowledge"},{"text":"Gem Valuer"}],[{"text":"Gem Trading"},{"text":"Gemology + commerce"},{"text":"Gemstone Buyer"}],[{"text":"Ethical Sourcing"},{"text":"Traceability + sourcing"},{"text":"Responsible Sourcing Specialist"}],[{"text":"Gemstone Research"},{"text":"Science + microscopy"},{"text":"Gemmological Researcher"}]]}]},{"heading":"Specialised Gemmology Training","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is one of the most important steps for this career."},{"type":"p","text":"Consider recognised gemmology programmes offered by established institutions and laboratories, depending on the intended specialisation."},{"type":"p","text":"Relevant study areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Foundation Gemmology"},{"text":"Coloured Stone Gemmology"},{"text":"Diamond Grading"},{"text":"Gem Identification"},{"text":"Gemstone Treatments"},{"text":"Gemmological Laboratory Techniques"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Internationally recognised gemmological qualifications can be valuable for professionals seeking laboratory or international jewellery-industry careers."},{"type":"p","text":"Before enrolling, verify:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Practical laboratory hours"},{"text":"Instrument training"},{"text":"Examination structure"},{"text":"Industry recognition"},{"text":"Current accreditation/status"},{"text":"Whether the qualification covers natural, synthetic and treated materials"}]}]},{"heading":"Gemmological Instruments","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional gemologist should learn the correct use and limitations of relevant instruments."},{"type":"h","text":"Core instruments"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"10× loupe"},{"text":"Gem microscope"},{"text":"Refractometer"},{"text":"Polariscope"},{"text":"Dichroscope"},{"text":"Spectroscope"},{"text":"Specific-gravity equipment"},{"text":"UV lamp"},{"text":"Diamond tester"},{"text":"Chelsea filter where applicable"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced laboratory equipment"},{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the laboratory:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UV-Vis spectroscopy"},{"text":"FTIR"},{"text":"Raman spectroscopy"},{"text":"Photoluminescence"},{"text":"X-ray-related analytical techniques"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A critical principle is:"},{"type":"p","text":"No single handheld tester should normally be treated as sufficient proof of gemstone identity or treatment."},{"type":"p","text":"Professional identification relies on multiple observations and tests interpreted together."}]},{"heading":"Internships","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gem laboratories"},{"text":"Diamond laboratories"},{"text":"Jewellery manufacturers"},{"text":"Jewellery brands"},{"text":"Gemstone dealers"},{"text":"Jewellery exporters"},{"text":"Auction houses"},{"text":"Jewellery quality-control departments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Search for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gemmology Intern"},{"text":"Gemstone Identification Trainee"},{"text":"Gem Lab Trainee"},{"text":"Diamond Grading Trainee"},{"text":"Jewellery QA Intern"},{"text":"Gemstone Research Intern"},{"text":"Gemstone Buyer Trainee"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong internship experience"},{"type":"p","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gemstone sorting"},{"text":"Identification"},{"text":"Microscopy"},{"text":"Diamond grading"},{"text":"Treatment detection"},{"text":"Laboratory documentation"},{"text":"Quality control"},{"text":"Gem procurement"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Gemstone Identification & Quality-Control Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Select a representative sample set."},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 1 — Visual examination"},{"type":"p","text":"Record:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Transparency"},{"text":"Lustre"},{"text":"Cut"},{"text":"Shape"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 2 — Instrument testing"},{"type":"p","text":"Use appropriate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Refractometer"},{"text":"Polariscope"},{"text":"Dichroscope"},{"text":"Spectroscope"},{"text":"Microscope"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 3 — Classification"},{"type":"p","text":"Classify specimens as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Natural"},{"text":"Synthetic"},{"text":"Simulant"},{"text":"Treated"}]},{"type":"p","text":"where the available evidence supports such a conclusion."},{"type":"h","text":"Stage 4 — Report"},{"type":"p","text":"Prepare a professional report containing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gem identification"},{"text":"Tests performed"},{"text":"Observations"},{"text":"Limitations"},{"text":"Treatment indicators"},{"text":"Final conclusion"}]}]},{"heading":"Diamond Specialisation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"If the student wants to work in the diamond industry, develop separate expertise."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"h","text":"4Cs:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cut"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Clarity"},{"text":"Carat weight"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Also understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Proportions"},{"text":"Fluorescence"},{"text":"Inclusions"},{"text":"Grading reports"},{"text":"Natural diamonds"},{"text":"Laboratory-grown diamonds"},{"text":"Diamond simulants"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Career options"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diamond Grader"},{"text":"Diamond Assessor"},{"text":"Diamond Buyer"},{"text":"Diamond Quality Analyst"},{"text":"Diamond Laboratory Specialist"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Diamond grading and laboratory work generally require dedicated training beyond a general design degree."}]},{"heading":"Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Entry-level"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gemmology Trainee"},{"text":"Junior Gemologist"},{"text":"Gemstone Identification Assistant"},{"text":"Diamond Grading Trainee"},{"text":"Jewellery Quality-Control Assistant"},{"text":"Gem Lab Assistant"},{"text":"Gemstone Buyer Assistant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Professional"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gemologist"},{"text":"Diamond Grader"},{"text":"Coloured Stone Gemologist"},{"text":"Gem Lab Analyst"},{"text":"Gemstone Quality Specialist"},{"text":"Jewellery Quality Specialist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Senior"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Gemologist"},{"text":"Senior Laboratory Gemologist"},{"text":"Gemstone Technical Specialist"},{"text":"Gemstone Procurement Specialist"},{"text":"Gemmology Consultant"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Leadership"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gem Lab Manager"},{"text":"Head Gemologist"},{"text":"Technical Head"},{"text":"Gemmology Consultant"},{"text":"Jewellery Quality Director"}]}]},{"heading":"Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Expect questions such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is gemmology?"},{"text":"How do you identify an unknown gemstone?"},{"text":"What is refractive index?"},{"text":"What is birefringence?"},{"text":"What is pleochroism?"},{"text":"What is specific gravity?"},{"text":"How do natural and synthetic gemstones differ?"},{"text":"What is a simulant?"},{"text":"What are common gemstone treatments?"},{"text":"How would you identify a treated stone?"},{"text":"Explain the diamond 4Cs."},{"text":"What is the difference between a laboratory-grown diamond and a diamond simulant?"},{"text":"Why is microscopy important?"},{"text":"Can one instrument conclusively identify every gemstone?"},{"text":"What information should appear in a professional gem report?"},{"text":"How would you handle uncertainty during identification?"},{"text":"Why is disclosure of treatments important?"},{"text":"How would you evaluate a gemstone before purchasing it?"}]}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Study in India","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Master's is not necessarily required for gemmology. Specialised practical gemmological training is generally more directly relevant."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential postgraduate directions include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Jewellery Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Des Jewellery Design"},{"text":"M.Des Accessory Design"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for combining:"},{"type":"h","text":"Gemmology + Jewellery Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Gemmology / Gem Sciences"},{"type":"p","text":"Where available:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gemmology"},{"text":"Gem Sciences"},{"text":"Jewellery Technology"},{"text":"Materials-related programmes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Materials Science"},{"type":"p","text":"Useful for research-oriented careers involving:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Gem materials"},{"text":"Synthetic materials"},{"text":"Characterisation"},{"text":"Advanced analytical techniques"}]}]},{"heading":"High-Value Specialist Routes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Route A — Laboratory Gemologist"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Gemmology","Instrumentation","Microscopy","Scientific Reporting"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential progression:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Trainee","Gemologist","Senior Gemologist","Lab Specialist","Lab Manager"]},{"type":"h","text":"Route B — Coloured Stone Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Gemmology","Mineralogy","Treatment Detection","Market Knowledge"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ruby"},{"text":"Sapphire"},{"text":"Emerald"},{"text":"Tourmaline"},{"text":"Spinel"},{"text":"Garnet"},{"text":"Other coloured gemstones"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route C — Diamond Specialist"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Diamond Grading","Gemmology","Market Knowledge"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Potential roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diamond Grader"},{"text":"Diamond Buyer"},{"text":"Diamond Quality Analyst"},{"text":"Laboratory Specialist"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route D — Gemstone Buyer"},{"type":"p","text":"Build:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Gemmology","Valuation","Market Intelligence","Sourcing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Pricing"},{"text":"Origin considerations"},{"text":"Treatment disclosure"},{"text":"Supplier evaluation"},{"text":"Market trends"},{"text":"Negotiation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route E — Jewellery Designer + Gemologist"},{"type":"p","text":"This is particularly relevant to a B.Des Jewellery/Accessory Design graduate."},{"type":"p","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Jewellery Design","Gemmology","CAD","Manufacturing"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The designer can make informed decisions about:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Stone selection"},{"text":"Cut"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Setting"},{"text":"Durability"},{"text":"Proportion"},{"text":"Jewellery construction"}]},{"type":"p","text":"This creates a stronger multidisciplinary profile than design or gemmology alone."}]},{"heading":"Gemstone Evaluation Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A professional workflow should be systematic:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Receive Specimen","Visual Examination","Weight / Dimensions","Microscopic Examination","Optical Testing","Specific Gravity / Other Tests","Spectral / Advanced Testing if Required","Natural / Synthetic / Simulant Assessment","Treatment Assessment","Interpret Results","Document Findings","Issue Appropriate Report"]},{"type":"p","text":"Where evidence is inconclusive, the correct professional response is to state the limitation or recommend additional testing, rather than force a definitive identification."}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Projects","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Gemstone Identification Catalogue"},{"type":"p","text":"Document 30+ gemstone specimens."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Natural vs Synthetic Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare representative natural and synthetic materials using appropriate observations and tests."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Treatment Study"},{"type":"p","text":"Document common treatment indicators across selected gemstones."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Diamond Grading Portfolio"},{"type":"p","text":"Create practice grading reports covering:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cut"},{"text":"Colour"},{"text":"Clarity"},{"text":"Carat"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Jewellery + Gemstone Collection"},{"type":"p","text":"Design a jewellery collection where each gemstone selection is technically justified."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 6 — Gemstone Buying Analysis"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare selected stones based on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Quality"},{"text":"Treatment"},{"text":"Durability"},{"text":"Market positioning"},{"text":"Intended jewellery use"}]}]},{"heading":"AI and the Future of Gemmology","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"AI and computer vision may increasingly support:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Inclusion image analysis"},{"text":"Pattern recognition"},{"text":"Spectral-data interpretation"},{"text":"Image classification"},{"text":"Gemstone database searching"},{"text":"Quality-control workflows"},{"text":"Inventory classification"},{"text":"Fraud detection"}]},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI should assist rather than replace qu